---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MediaCredit from "../components/MediaCredit.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import { asset } from "../data/paths";
---

<Layout title={`Accessibility & media credits — ${site.wordmark}`}>
  <div class="reading-container">
    <header class="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Access & attribution</p><h1>
        Accessibility & media credits
      </h1><p class="lead">The design target is WCAG 2.1 Level A and AA.</p><p>
        This author-maintained research site uses semantic HTML, a neutral
        palette, keyboard-operable controls, and descriptive alternatives for
        research media. Automated checks are part of the deployment workflow;
        they do not establish complete ADA or WCAG conformance.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <section>
        <h2>Using this site</h2><ul>
          <li>
            The first keyboard link skips to the main content. Keyboard focus is
            visible throughout the page.
          </li><li>
            Silent videos can start automatically when first visible and loop.
            Use “Pause videos” or native controls to stop playback. Scrolling
            the videos out of view pauses them; returning does not override a
            manual pause. Reduced-motion and data-saving preferences suppress
            automatic playback. Explicit playback remains available.
          </li><li>
            The NASA/Joby context clip and Flying DNA simulation clip have no audio tracks. Each has a complete
            HTML visual description and a timed WebVTT description track.
          </li><li>
            The title and authors appear above complete video frames. The
            videos stack vertically on narrow screens.
          </li><li>
            Paper figures have descriptive alternatives and longer explanations.
            Results appear as labeled values and structured tables, so color is
            not required to understand them.
          </li><li>
            At narrow widths, content reflows into a single column. Wide data
            tables and BibTeX text scroll within their own focusable areas.
          </li><li>
            Core content, all result comparisons, and native player controls
            remain available without JavaScript.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Flying DNA materials and research scope</h2><p>
          The authors’ six-slide <cite>Flying DNA - Copy 1.pptx</cite> introduces
          a project vision built around Digital Twin, Networked Systems, and Artificial
          Intelligence. These three pillars are distinct from the methods and results
          validated in the 2025 published eVTOL paper. Presentation material does
          not extend the paper’s experimental claims.
        </p><p>
          The selected stills show the digital-twin city and wind field from
          slide 5; both have alt text and complete HTML explanations. The right
          title video presents the complete slide 6 animation,
          <code>image13.gif</code>, as an original-speed, silent MP4 with
          playback controls. The source presentation remains unchanged and is
          not republished as a complete attachment.
        </p><p>
          The left title video is existing NASA/Joby real-flight footage. It and
          the presentation simulation come from separate sources, not the same
          experiment. Neither demonstrates a real-aircraft trial of this paper’s
          controller. Full visual descriptions and source credits appear below.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="attachments">
        <h2>Papers, figures & data attachments</h2><p>
          The <a href={asset("paper/")}>HTML research guide</a> is a companion to
          the paper, not its complete text. <a href={asset("results/")}
            >HTML result tables and figure descriptions</a
          > accompany the downloadable CSV data and images.
        </p><p>
          The supplied Elsevier PDF reports that it contains tags. Tag presence
          alone does not verify heading structure, figure alternatives, equation
          reading, or reading order. We link to the publisher’s version of
          record, whose full-text availability may depend on access rights.
        </p><p>
          The original uploaded PDF has not been altered or republished here. We
          have not certified external PDF reading order, mathematical
          accessibility, or assistive-technology behavior. CSV files are plain
          data; the HTML tables provide captions and row/column headers.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>External related work</h2><p>
          GeoWind2Plan is related work by independent authors. Its
          <a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.36056v1">HTML preprint</a> and
          <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2609.36056v1">GeoWind2Plan PDF</a> are linked
          for further reading; its findings are not presented as this project’s experiments.
        </p><p>
          The external GeoWind2Plan PDF is untagged, and its reading order and
          assistive-technology behavior have not been verified. The HTML version
          provides another reading format, without a claim of complete
          accessibility conformance.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Checks and remaining review</h2><p>
          The repository includes an axe-core check against WCAG 2.1 A/AA rules,
          plus checks for keyboard navigation, media behavior, image
          alternatives, 320 CSS-pixel reflow, text spacing, and content with
          JavaScript disabled. A failing check blocks automatic deployment. See <a
            href={`${site.siteRepo}/actions`}>the deployment checks</a
          > and <a href={`${site.siteRepo}/blob/main/ACCESSIBILITY.md`}
            >the review record</a
          >.
        </p><p>
          The 18 October revision checks controlled automatic playback,
          keyboard pause and play, persistent manual pause, reduced-motion and
          data-saving preferences, complete media frames, and 320 CSS-pixel
          reflow. Detailed outcomes are recorded in the repository review record.
        </p><p>
          Automated coverage is limited. A full review with multiple screen
          readers, users with disabilities, and institutional accessibility and
          brand reviewers remains outside the completed technical checks. This
          page does not claim an ADA or WCAG certification.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Report an access barrier</h2><p>
          Email <a href="mailto:liusongyang@ufl.edu"
            >Songyang Liu at liusongyang@ufl.edu</a
          >. Please include the page, the content you need, and the browser or
          assistive technology involved so we can help provide a usable format.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Privacy</h2><p>
          This static site loads its fonts, figures, and short video excerpts
          locally. It uses no analytics, advertising, or embedded third-party
          players. Following an external link opens the provider’s site, where
          that provider’s privacy practices apply.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <div class="section"><MediaCredit /></div>
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Research figure credits</h2><p>
        Selected figures come from the user-supplied published paper by {
          site.authors.map((a) => a.name).join(", ")
        }. Figure numbers, original third-party credits where present, and
        descriptive explanations appear on the <a
          href={asset("results/#figures")}>results and figures page</a
        >. Rights in published papers and third-party media remain with their
        respective holders.
      </p><p>
        The additional city and wind-field stills come from slide 5 of the
        authors’ Flying DNA presentation. The original scientific diagram colors
        are retained as research content; labels
        and text alternatives explain the information without requiring color
        identification.
      </p>{
        site.id === "eVTOL_webpage" && (
          <p>
            Figure 7 uses city geometry from{" "}
            <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">
              OpenStreetMap contributors
            </a>
            .
          </p>
        )
      }
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
